That makes a lot of sense to me.  And I prefer the suffix to
another <...> argument.

We also need things like differences of CDFs for full
truncation:

  normal_diff_lcdf(y_low, y_high, mu, sigma)

  =def= log(normal_cdf(y_high,mu,sigma) - normal_cdf(y_low,mu,sigma))

Right now, it's being implemented as above, but it could really
use better implementations.  Then we could think about vectorizing
the truncated densities.

> Also if optional arguments are allowed as normal_lpdf<norm=true>, why not then have also link functions as optional arguments, e.g.,
>  bernoulli_lpdf<link=probit> or bernoulli_lpdf<link=logit> or bernoulli_lpdf<link=linear> ?

We could.  I don't want to get carried away and in particular don't
want expressions as values of those = things --- just template
parameters that resolve which function is called.

- Bob

