Oh, and the reason I don't like normal_pdf and that
I do like the vertical bar is that it is what you see
in stats papers for the function:

  cauchy(y | mu, tau)

But on the log scale, we don't want to write

  log cauchy(y | mu, tau)   or log(cauchy(y | mu, tau))

because it's two functions (though I suppose I could fish it
out of the abstract syntax tree and reduce it during code
generation).

- Bob

