The stas paper also use ~, which has been considered problematic in Stan.

If we have
 << normal(y | mu, sigma)
do we then have, e.g. (toy example)
 << normal(y | mu, sigma), normal_cdf(y_high,mu,sigma) - normal_cdf(y_low,mu,sigma)
or
 << normal(y | mu, sigma), log(normal_cdf(y_high,mu,sigma) - normal_cdf(y_low,mu,sigma))
another example
 << normal(y | mu, sigma), 1/sigma
or
 << normal(y | mu, sigma), -log(sigma)

I would love to use notation close to stats papers, but I don't see yet how we obtain consistency when combining built-in distributions and other expressions when using ~ or <<

