Maybe.  It'll also break people's old code.

The one thing we have to fight strongly against is forking.
If things change enough, people will just lock in whatever 2.x
they're using and not update.  Just look at what happened
to Python and is now happening to Julia.

Luckily,  unlike those two languages, people probably haven't
built packages around RStan, PyStan, etc., other than us anyway.

- Bob

