On Wednesday, January 6, 2016 at 5:09:29 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> As to inverse CDFs, you're right that it doesn't make sense to have log
> output.  But what about logit input?  Or do we have complementary inverse
> cdfs to deal with the overflow to 1 problem on the 1 side of (0,1)?

R has an option for log input, but I don't think it is that big a deal for Stan. If the probability is nearly 0 or 1, then the inverse CDF will probably not be very stable even if we give it more stable input.

Ben

