Sorry to confuse the issue --- I meant "_lpdf" or "_pdf", not "_log".

I don't want users to be able to write a "shorthand" and "longhand"
version of the same function.  Let's just pick one and stick with it.

Stan's parser won't care about whitespaces and will let you write
any foolish syntactic convention you want (other than foregoing semicolons
[a la R] or dropping parens in favor of indenting [a la Python]).

But if you count the spaces in "normal(a, b, c)" and "normal(a | b, c)"
you'll see that the latter is one character wider.  Size matters.  As
does having enough space between things to read.

- Bob

