I don't want "normal" to be an abbreviation for anything.

Either the function to compute the log pdf is "normal(y | mu, sigma)"
or it's "normal_lpdf(y | mu, sigma)" or it's something else.

Allowing both is going to be very confusing to users.  They'll
immediately come to the conclusion there's a difference and try to
figure out which one they should use.

- Bob

