Just a heads up; as of a couple of days ago Github recognizes Stan language files and will highlight them (see https://github.com/github/linguist/pull/2809). Github uses the Ruby package linguist (https://github.com/github/linguist) for their syntax highlighting and language detection.  For the syntax highlighting itself it uses grammar for Stan that I wrote for an Atom package: https://github.com/jrnold/atom-language-stan. This means that you should also be able to get syntax highlighting in markdown files as rendered on Github.

