> >    @ += <expression>;
> >
> >    where @ is just shorthand for target since it looks a bit like a
> >    target. Just using target is probably better, but thought I'd throw it
> >    out there.
>
> Have we considered whitespace indent level (like python)? It might make
> more sense here than it does even in python because users almost always
> want to increment the log probability. Since users are generally in the
> habit of indenting to the appropriate level already, that might be a
> least effort and least visually noisy way to indicate it.
>
> $0.02
>
> I'm vetoing using whitespace indent levels.
>
> some reasons:
> 1) not backwards compatible
> 2) users are still jamming everything in strings without any care to indentation
> 3) ... no. I can't deal with it.
