> Yes I think _lp should appended, so normal_lp() and normal_cdf_lp(). Levels of detail:

I could live with _lp referring either to the log of a PDF or a PMF but normal_cdf_lp() seems really weird to me. A CDF is already returning a probability and even if you put in on the log scale, what additional information is the trailing p supposed to convey? I get that poisson_log_log() is bad but poisson_loglink_log() is not so bad (just long). Although I don't mind typing more characters at all if we can convey the meanings to users more clearly.

Ben

