Yeah, and RStudio (maybe R in general, I forget) will bring up suggestions if you type x$partial and there's an element in x whose name starts with "partial". But instead of making you use one of the suggestions (or letting it autocomplete) you are allowed to just use x$partial. This makes it quite dangerous to use "$" when writing code for an R package (which I've learned the hard way a few times).

There are also some weird rules about when the names are too ambiguous for the partial matching, but it's hard to remember those and the documentation is pretty abysmal.

