Right --- in the simplest case, we get a beta-binomial prior.
But in practice, the bigger the parameters to the beta part of
it, the better, assuming we have the right mean.  And the sky's
the limit here (actually, the binomial's the limit).

>> It's just semantics, like whether we call something concentrated
>> or peaky or precise or sharp or pointy.  Or like deciding whether
