It’s simpler because you chose a model that’s so easy there
is no confusion!  Add some nonlinear transformations to LHS
or any of the distributions, or try to add a discrete distribution
over parameters to the target.  The @ notation has no intuition
and absolutely no context.  Defaulting to log pdfs makes the
notation symmetric and hides what’s really going on.

The first is not hard to read, the additional time needed to write
it and potential for typos is minimal, especially with automatic
code completion.

