 I like the Stan language because it lets me express a probabilistic model without much ambiguity while automating the numerical stuff. I know other people appreciate the BUGS-like veneer it places over MCMC.  Maybe if we want BUGS level of simplicity, we should do a language subset that deals only in graphical models and either keep the ~ syntax or use @ for that. If we did an rStanBUGS interface I'm sure we could nab a bigger user base...

