I'm finding it very difficult to figure out where I stand on this issue.

On one hand, I completely agree with Michael (and others) about the value of making existing ambiguities explicit. On the other hand, like Bob says, I am also quite worried that we risk alienating many current and future users, and I do think the proposed changes to the language are quite hideous from an aesthetic point of view. I agree with Michael that I don't think they will make Stan programs _harder_ to read, but I do think they make them uglier. But how much value we should place in aesthetics I'm really not sure.

I wonder if it would be helpful (or at a minimum interesting) to ask current users for feedback on these proposed changes. I'm not at all proposing that we blindly do what current users want, but we're hypothesizing about their reactions without really asking.

