On Thursday, January 28, 2016 at 2:45:55 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> So just to clarify, it's not that Python users don't like Stan
> because it's a domain-specific language.  They don't like it because
> it's not an *embedded* domain specific language where the embedding
> is in Python.  See:

Right. Anyway, if there is something else --- in addition to changing the Stan language --- that is easy-ish and not overly platform specific which would allow a large subset of users to specify models using a large subset of the Stan language, that would be good. That is pretty much what rstanarm / brms / rethinking are doing, although they are R specific. If so, then perhaps we could change the Stan language in a direction that would appeal to the complementary set of users.

Ben

